# Reference

Formats, schemas, and tables for the principled-extraction pipeline.

## Taxonomy

Classify each unit by purpose. The litmus test picks the type.

| Type | Litmus test | Destination |
|---|---|---|
| theory | A claim about the world | `claims.md` with a source tag and confidence |
| concept | A portable idea, not checkable on a diff | `concepts.md` |
| applicable | A way to execute something: interface or snippet | `applicable/` |
| rule | A reviewer returns PASS or FAIL on a diff | `rules-candidates.md` |

Source tags: `vendor` (the round author), `independent` (a third party), `our-empirical` (a run in this workspace). Tag every unit.

## P-1 policy card

Ask once. Return one card. This is the only human input.

```
Model budget:    paid | free-only | mixed
                 paid is the default. mixed splits the roles, example:
                 paid -> extract, skeptic, synth
                 free -> recon, classify
Web research:    yes | no
Rule policy:     pending-only | auto-should | never
Round folder:    <path to materials in AGENTIC_PAPERS/rounds-research/>
Output:          AGENTIC_PAPERS/principles&ideas/<round>/
```

Rule policy:

- `pending-only`: write `rules-candidates.md` as `pending`. Leave the catalog alone.
- `auto-should`: write corroborated `our-empirical` candidates with `severity: should`.
- `never`: skip the rules bucket.

Web research `no` marks every theory `uncorroborated`.

## Layout

Two folders, never mixed:

```
AGENTIC_PAPERS/
  rounds-research/<round>/        materials only (source docs). No EXTRACTS here.
  principles&ideas/<round>/       results + README + process/
    README.md                     index + practical takeaway
    claims.md  concepts.md  rules-candidates.md  applicable/
    process/                      recon, preflight, raw/classified/skeptic/dedup json, session-graph
```

One round folder per round. Do not scatter result files at the `principles&ideas/` root.

## Roles and models

Pre-fill from `monster-longrun/MODEL-CATALOG.md`. The owner may override any role. Every paid id below must resolve in `subagent({action:"models"})` at preflight.

| Node | Role | Paid (default) | Free (opt-in) | Thinking | Required tools |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| P0 | Scout | `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash` | `openrouter/nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` | low | `ls`, `read` |
| P1 | Extractor | `deepseek/deepseek-flash` | `openrouter/qwen/qwen3.8-27b:free` | low | `read`, `write` |
| P2 | Classifier | `deepseek/deepseek-flash` | `openrouter/qwen/qwen3.8-27b:free` | low | `read`, `write` |
| P3 | Corroborator | `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash` | none | low | `web_search`, `web_read` |
| P4 | Skeptic | `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro` | `openrouter/thinkingmachines/inkling:free` | off | `read` |
| P6 | Synthesizer | `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro` | `kimi-coding/kimi-for-coding` | off | `read`, `write` |

A role is a triple: task, model, tool-set. A subagent without its required tool does not run that node. P0 and P3 fall to the Conductor when no subagent carries the tool. Run P3 as a different agent from P1: a claim's extractor does not verify its own claim.

## Preflight checklist

Run at P-1, before P0. A failure here stops the run; it does not degrade silently.

1. **Models.** Call `subagent({action:"models"})`. Every role model in the table must appear exactly in the registry. `:free` variants are separate ids; the catalog is a claim, the registry is the fact.
2. **Tools.** At spawn, confirm each role carries its required tools. Required tool missing: Conductor owns P0/P3, the run stops for P1/P2/P4/P6.
3. **Catalog hash.** `sha256sum ~/.agents/skills/to-violations/PRINCIPLES.md`. Write the hash to the run log. P7 compares it; `mtime` is not proof.
4. **Budget.** Record `timeoutMs` per role. Use 8 minutes for P1, P2, P6.

## Fallback policy

- Paid is the default. Free is opt-in per role at P-1.
- A free role that fails twice (error, empty output, or a repeated tool call) switches once to its paid model, same task, fresh context.
- A paid role never falls back to free.
- Two failures on the paid model stop the run. A free role stops after two failures if no paid model is set.
- Treat an upstream 429 on a shared free pool as a failure, not a rate limit of ours.

## Output schemas

### claims.md

```
| id | claim | source_tag | corroborated | confidence | quote | location |
```

### concepts.md

```
| id | concept | source_tag | why it travels | quote | location |
```

### applicable/

One file per interface or pattern. Include a short snippet and the source line.

### rules-candidates.md

```
# Rule candidates, status: pending

| id | name | severity | source_tag | corroborated | quote | location |
```

Use the id prefix `TS-` for this round. Cap severity at `should`. Dedup against `~/.agents/skills/to-violations/PRINCIPLES.md` before writing. Report each match by catalog id.

### session-graph.jsonl

One line per phase, gate, and subagent. Follow the Ralph telemetry contract. Reuse `~/.agents/skills/monster-longrun/scripts/session-graph.mjs`. Set `trace_id` to the run id.

## Gate format

A gate is a command plus an expected result.

```
Gate: grep -c '^| TS-' AGENTIC_PAPERS/principles&ideas/<round>/rules-candidates.md
Expect: an integer >= 1

Gate: sha256sum ~/.agents/skills/to-violations/PRINCIPLES.md
Expect: the hash recorded at P-1
```

Run each gate yourself, in the Conductor. A subagent report is data, not authority. Re-parse the output file and recount; do not trust a summary.

## Catalog merge

The run stops at `pending`. Merging into `PRINCIPLES.md` is a separate session. The human approves each rule. After a merge, run `principles-render` twice and check the diff is empty.
